  "body": "## What happens\n\nPer-post script options stored with `set_post_options { \"script_options\": ... }` (#258) are dropped without a word when the MCP `post` tool is given a `post` name. That includes naming the post the document already uses. The same document posted without a `post` name applies them.\n\n## Reproduction (main 4b7a6b1e, `camcraft-cli mcp`)\n\n```json\n[[\"load_machine\", {\"builtin\": \"VMC 3-axis\"}],\n [\"set_stock\", {\"box\": {\"dx\": 60, \"dy\": 40, \"dz\": 10}}],\n [\"add_tool\", {\"catalog\": \"EM-1000-4FL\"}],\n [\"add_operation\", {\"kind\": \"face\", \"tool\": \"EM-1000-4FL\", \"name\": \"F1\"}],\n [\"generate\", {}],\n [\"set_post_options\", {\"script_options\": {\"showSequenceNumbers\": \"every-block\", \"writeToolList\": true, \"safeRetract\": \"G53\"}}],\n [\"post\", {\"output\": \"named.nc\", \"post\": \"Fanuc\"}],\n [\"post\", {\"output\": \"doc.nc\"}]]\n```\n\n`set_post_options` answers with `\"post\": \"Fanuc (built-in)\"` and the three options set. Both posts succeed with no warning.\n\n`doc.nc` (no `post` named) has them:\n\n```\nO0001 (VMC 3-AXIS)\n(T1 - FLAT END MILL D10. EM-1000-4FL)\nN10 G21\n...\nN340 G53 G00 Z0.\nN350 M30\n```\n\n`named.nc` (`\"post\": \"Fanuc\"`) has none of them: no N words, no tool list, and the default `G28` retract instead of the chosen `G53`.\n\nThe same happens with `useRadiusArcs: true` on a round waterline pocket. `\"post\": \"Fanuc\"` writes every arc with I/J, byte-identical to the option off.\n\n## Root cause (confirmed)\n\n`posting::program_options_for_script` merges the stored options only when it is given the post:\n\n```rust\nlet mut overrides = post\n    .map(|p| crate::setup_post_options::script_for_post(world, setup, p))\n    .unwrap_or_default();\n```\n\nThe MCP `post` tool calls `script::api::v_post`. With a `cps` given, that goes through `posting_mounts::post_mounts_script_with_options` → `posting::post_script_with_script_options`, which calls `post_script_as(..., None, None, extra)`. With `post: None` the stored options are never read. Only `extra` would apply: `v_post`'s `options` key, which the MCP `post` tool does not expose.\n\n## Expected\n\nWhen the named post is one the stored options belong to (here, the document's own Fanuc), those options apply, as they do with no name given. Otherwise the post says it did not apply them; it must not drop the user's `safeRetract` or arc form unseen.\n\n## Suggested labels\n\nOutside contributors can't set labels, so these are suggestions:\n\n- `P3`: a set option that silently does nothing on one path.\n- `effort:medium`\n- `area:post`\n- `area:mcp`\n- `source:agent`\n\n🤖 Generated with [Claude Code](https://claude.com/claude-code)\n",
